   "subject": "Re: Survival analysis in INLA",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi Jonesmus,<br><br>The coefficients represent the increase in the expected log hazard for each covariate. You can get summary statistics for exp(coefficients) instead of coefficients (i.e. hazard ratios) by adding the following argument to the summary function: summary(model1, hazr=TRUE). Then the null effect is 1 and an effect is statistically significant at a significance level of 0.05 when the 95% credible interval does not contain 1.<br><br>Best,<br>Denis Rustand<br><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">he...@r-inla.org</a>"
    ],
    [
     3,
